#let items = (
 p(1,"E","U1 Cancellation",[State the definition of epimorphism and prove every surjective set function is epic.],[Compare two maps after precomposition.],[Evaluate at a preimage of each target element.],[An arrow $e:A -> B$ is epic if $u e=v e$ implies $u=v$ for all parallel maps out of $B$. If $e$ is a surjective function, choose for each $b$ any $a$ with $e(a)=b$. Then $u(b)=u(e(a))=v(e(a))=v(b)$. Thus $u=v$.],[No simultaneous choice of preimages is needed; argue for an arbitrary $b$.]),
 p(2,"E","U4 Universal properties",[State the coproduct property and identify the coproduct of two finite sets of sizes three and four.],[Use tagged injections.],[The resulting set has seven elements.],[The coproduct is a tagged disjoint union of size seven. For maps from the two sets to any $X$, define the mediating function on each tagged component by the given map. It is unique because every element belongs to exactly one component.],[Include the maps and uniqueness clause.]),
 p(3,"C","U3 Naturality",[Prove the swap maps $X times X -> X times X$, $(x,y)|->(y,x)$ form a natural isomorphism.],[Check a general function $f:X -> Y$.],[Both square paths send $(x,y)$ to $(f(y),f(x))$.],[For any $f:X->Y$, both $(f times f)"swap"_X$ and $"swap"_Y(f times f)$ send $(x,y)$ to $(f(y),f(x))$, proving naturality. Each swap composed with itself is the identity, so each component is invertible; the inverse family is the same natural transformation. Thus it is a natural isomorphism.],[Check naturality and invertibility independently.]),
