 p(6,"A","U7–U8 Adjunctions",[Prove a left adjoint preserves initial objects directly from its hom-set bijection.],[Count maps from the image of an initial object.],[The corresponding source hom set is a singleton.],[If $I$ is initial in $cal(C)$ and $F tack.l G$, then for every $D$ the adjunction gives $cal(D)(F I,D) iso cal(C)(I,G D)$. The right set has exactly one element, so the left does too. This is precisely initiality of $F I$.],[Use all targets $D$, not one particular object.]),
